# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
venv/
.venv/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.installed.cfg
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored `lib/`, `build/` and `dist/`
# are Python packaging patterns that also swallow real frontend source —
# `frontend/src/lib/utils.ts` was ignored-but-tracked because of exactly that.
/build/*
# ...except the installer icon. electron-builder finds it by convention rather
# than by a path in electron-builder.yml, so a clone without it produces an
# installer wearing the default Electron icon — silently, with nothing failing.
# It is generated output like the brand PNGs under frontend/public/, and it is
# tracked for the same reason: the build must not depend on someone having run
# the generator first. Regenerate with scripts/build-brand-assets.py.
!/build/icon.ico
# The uninstaller's data questions. Source, not build output — without it the
# uninstaller silently keeps everything and "remove completely" is unavailable.
!/build/installer.nsh
/dist/
/develop-eggs/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/

# Testing & linting caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# IDE — personal settings stay local, but settings.json is shared project
# config (it keeps Pylance out of frontend/ and the venvs) so it is committed.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment — never commit keys
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
desktop/dist/
packages/*/dist/
dist-electron/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The Spine — the user's local knowledge base. User data, never committed.
spine.db
spine.db-journal
spine.db-wal
spine.db-shm
backend/spine.db*

# The egress log and its policy. A record of every question that left the
# machine is the most private file Zaram holds — more so than the Spine, which
# at least only contains what the user chose to store. Never committed.
egress.db
egress.db-journal
egress.db-wal
egress.db-shm
backend/egress.db*
egress-policy.json
backend/egress-policy.json

# Backend-side user settings — the chosen model and the routing preference.
# Written beside the egress policy and ignored for the same reason: it is the
# user's configuration of their own machine, and committing one developer's
# choice of model would silently become everybody's default.
settings.json
backend/settings.json

# Artifact records, and the files they describe. Both are the user's own work —
# their invoices, proposals and client spreadsheets. The database holds the
# provenance and the full HTML of every document generated, which makes it as
# private as the Spine, and the output directory holds the documents themselves.
artifacts.db
artifacts.db-journal
artifacts.db-wal
artifacts.db-shm
backend/artifacts.db*
backend/generated/

# Ingest records: which folders the user pointed at, every file in them, and
# what was extracted. The paths alone describe someone's whole working life —
# clients, projects, what they are being paid — so this is as private as the
# Spine and belongs next to it, not in the repo.
ingest.db
ingest.db-journal
ingest.db-wal
ingest.db-shm
backend/ingest.db*

# Screenshots from driving the interface. Reproduce them by running the script;
# committing them means a binary diff on every UI change and a stale picture in
# the repo the day after.
frontend/scripts/drive-shots/

# Generated audio. Produced by the speech runtime at runtime, not source.
backend/audio/
backend/audio_clips/
backend/audio_output/
# The Kokoro provider's own cache. Missed by the list above because nothing had
# actually synthesised speech on a working tree until 10 August 2026 — the
# directory only appears once the model runs. `pyproject.toml` already excludes
# it from test collection, which is where the omission hid.
backend/audio_cache/

# Uploads — whatever the user dropped in. Never ours to commit.
uploads/

# AI tool scratch space. Session artefacts, vendored skill bundles and
# worktrees, none of which are Zaram source.
.playwright-mcp/
.kilo/skills/
.kilo/worktrees/

# Ad-hoc captures and command output. Screenshots that are part of the
# design record live in docs/design/ and are committed deliberately.
/*.png
/*.log
/*.jpg
tsc_out*
lint_out*
zaram-current-state*
frontend/screenshot*.png

# Retired surface, kept on disk only. The name uses vocabulary CLAUDE.md
# retired; nothing in it is referenced by the build.
zaram-ai-operating-system-ui/

# Test VRM avatars. Large binaries, and the sample is a licensed VRoid
# export rather than ours to redistribute.
*.vrm

# Projects — the user's own project records, like the Spine and artifacts.
backend/projects.db
backend/projects.db-wal
backend/projects.db-shm

# Code signing material. A committed certificate is a revoked certificate:
# once the private key is in git history it is compromised, and the only
# remedy is reissuing — paid for again, and re-validated from scratch.
#
# Since 2023 a publicly-trusted signing key must live on a hardware token or
# an HSM, so a .pfx in the repo should not exist at all. These patterns are
# here for the ones that do anyway: test certificates, exported backups, and
# whatever a future self downloads "just to try it".
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.spc
*.pvk
.signing/
signing-*.json

# Brand preview sheets. `scripts/build-brand-assets.py` writes them beside the
# source image so a preview can never land in `frontend/public/`, which ships.
# They are regenerated from the same definition as the real assets, so tracking
# them would put a rebuildable PNG in every diff that touches the mark.
Logo_Image/_preview.png

# The bundled Python runtime. ~300 MB of third-party CPython plus the backend's
# dependencies, assembled by scripts/build-python-runtime.mjs and rebuilt from
# a pinned release rather than tracked. Committing it would put a vendored
# interpreter in every clone and in every diff.
/runtime/
/.runtime-download/
